        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: a serra",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "a serra — \"the mountain range, the hills; the saw\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Passámos o fim de semana na serra. We spent the weekend in the mountains."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A ridge of peaks looks like the teeth of a saw. Serrar — to saw."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "serra is inherited from Latin serra 'saw' (EtymDB): a mountain ridge has the jagged outline of a saw's teeth."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
